Package: webdavfs
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Bizzgit <bizzgit@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: fuse, logrotate
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/Bizzgit/webdavfs
Description: FUSE filesystem for WebDAV shares (mount.webdavfs)
 Fork of miquels/webdavfs. Mounts a WebDAV share through FUSE without a
 local cache, so it can be used from /etc/fstab or a systemd mount unit
 as filesystem type webdavfs.
 .
 Installs /usr/sbin/mount.webdavfs and a logrotate rule for the optional
 trace file (the tracefile= mount option).
 .
 Upgrading replaces the binary but does not remount: a running mount keeps
 using the old binary until it is mounted again, so an upgrade never
 interrupts a mounted share. Removing the package removes mount.webdavfs,
 and an /etc/fstab entry of type webdavfs then fails to mount at the next
 boot.
